# Desktop apps. All free. Work-managed apps (JumpCloud, Falcon, VPN, Slack, Zoom) are IT's and not here.
# Browsers (Brave default, Chrome as a test target) are hand-installed: their own updaters lock
# the bundles, so Homebrew cannot adopt or replace them. The checklist covers a fresh machine.
# Third-party tap: Homebrew 7 loads nothing from it until trusted; trust the one item, not the tap.
tap "menubar-apps/menubar-apps"

# Launcher, clipboard history, snippets (replaces Spotlight, Maccy)
cask "raycast"
# Screenshots: annotate, OCR, measure. Cmd-Shift-2
cask "shottr"
# Cmd-Tab with per-window previews (install.sh moves its hold key from Option to Command)
cask "alt-tab"
# Quick todo list in the menu bar
cask "menubar-apps/menubar-apps/todobar", trusted: true
# Archives, full uninstalls
cask "keka"
cask "appcleaner"
# Notes, if ever wanted (markdown on disk, free)
# cask "obsidian"
